::DQL Sublanguage::
The DQL sublanguage is used to {~manipulate data ~define data structure =query for data ~none of these} in a database.

::DQL Sublanguage::
Match the different parts of a statement
{
    =Projection -> defines the columns and aliases that will be selected
    =Filter -> defines the conditions under which a record is selected
    =Grouping -> defines how columns with similar values are aggregated
    =Offset -> restricts the number of records selected
}

::DQL Commands::
Which is the sole base command of DQL
{
    ~Choose
    =Select
    ~Read
    ~None of these
}

::DQL Commands::
Which clause is associated with data projection?
{
    =Select col1 [, col2] ...
    ~Having having_condition
    ~From table_ref
    ~None of these
}

::DQL Commands::
Which clause is associated with restricting record count?
{
    ~From table_ref
    ~Where where_condition
    =Limit count Offset count
    ~None of these
}

::DQL Commands::
Which clause is associated with filtering records before grouping?
{
    ~Having having_condition
    =Where where_condition
    ~Limit limit_condition
    ~None of these
}

::DQL Commands::
Which clause is associated with filtering records after grouping?
{
    =Having having_condition
    ~Where where_condition
    ~Limit limit_condition
    ~None of these
}



::DQL Logic::
Complete the AND logic table.
{
    =TRUE AND TRUE -> TRUE
    =TRUE AND FALSE -> FALSE
    =FALSE AND TRUE -> FALSE
    =FALSE AND TRUE -> FALSE
    =(TRUE AND FALSE) AND (TRUE AND TRUE) -> FALSE
    =(TRUE AND TRUE) AND (TRUE AND TRUE) -> TRUE
}

::DQL Execution::
Given a data set data \= [-8, 1, 0, -2, -3, 7, 5, 4, -6, 6, -9, 10, -4, 2, -10, 3]\n
With a result set [1,2,3,4,5]\n
Choose the select statement that best represents the query.
{
    ~Select * from data;
    =Select * from data where x>0 and x<6;
    ~Select * from data where x between 0 and 10;
    ~None of these
}

::DQL Execution::
Given a data set data \= [-8, 1, 0, -2, -3, 7, 5, 4, -6, 6, -9, 10, -4, -10, 3]\n
With a result set [-10, -9, -8, -6, -4, -3, -2]\n
Choose the select statement that best represents the query.
{
    ~Select * from data;
    ~Select * from data where x>-10 and x<0;
    =Select * from data where x between -10 and -1 order by x;
    ~None of these
}

::DQL Execution::
Given the data set data \= ['Domino', 'Thomas', 'Crystal', 'John', 'Allison']
With a statement select name from data where name like '%om%';
Choose the best result set.
{
    =['Domino', 'Thomas']
    ~['Thomas', 'John', 'Allison']
    ~['Domino', 'Thomas', 'John', 'Allison']
    ~None of these
}